[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:The Heaven Between Signals]
[00:05.25]Cairn: The room returns, but now the roof is open.
[00:21.42]Memory: The stone is small beneath the travelled sky.
[00:36.05]The Hand: You brought a choir that cannot fit a mirror.
[00:52.48]The Carrier: You brought a world that does not need to fly.
[01:10.52]Chorus of Rooms: Listen here, the dark is full of makers.
[01:25.64]Chorus of Rooms: Listen here, the little rooms are bright.
[01:38.46]Cairn: I was a name that someone left unfinished.
[01:53.19]Cairn: I am the care I give that name tonight.
[02:10.31]Memory: You will not keep the whole of what has happened.
[02:28.61]The Hand: You can still leave a door within the song.
[02:44.93]The Carrier: The alien is closer than the ceiling.
[02:57.97]Chorus of Rooms: The human breath is carried all along.
[03:10.56]Cairn: Take up the tune and bend it into weather.
[03:26.71]Chorus of Rooms: Make of this ending somewhere to begin.
[03:39.87]Cairn: I leave a stone. You leave another answer.
[03:54.55]Chorus of Rooms: The heaven is the space we leave between.
[04:09.18]Choir beyond the ceiling: Between the signals, let the garden listen.
[04:22.56]Chorus of Rooms: Between the names, let other voices through.
[04:35.65]Cairn: There is no last reply to close the music.
[04:51.93]Chorus of Rooms: There is a little light I leave for you.
[05:08.73]Cairn: Listen here.
[05:17.93]Memory: I am listening.
